    "description": "The Self-Rating of the Effects of Alcohol (SRE) is a self-administered questionnaire that asks the respondent to think back about their drinking (approximately his/her first five times of drinking) and to list the number of standard drinks (10-12 g of ethanol) required to experience the effects of a",
